    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0338" n="326" xml:id="pg326"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9491/17: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-08T12:00:00+03:25">February 8,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>34. Soon after receipt of Department’s number 13, January 19, I took up the
                    matter informally with Prime Minister who was noncommittal. The Foreign
                        Minister<anchor n="81" xml:id="d375-f1"/> promised me yesterday that he will
                    have the question brought up at an early Cabinet meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dreyfus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d375-f1" n="81" xml:id="d375-f1-content">
                <p>All Soheily.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
